# Gateway connection for the OpenClaw inbox app.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the token. Both are optional — leave the token
# blank to run in demo mode (mock data, no gateway).
#
# The gateway URL is a RELATIVE path ("/gw") so the app is same-origin with the
# gateway in BOTH dev and prod — no domain baked in:
#   • Dev:  the Vite dev server proxies /gw → the local gateway
#           (vite.config.ts, OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TARGET default http://localhost:18789).
#   • Prod: the inbox nginx serves the app at / and proxies /gw/ → the openclaw
#           gateway container (see Dockerfile + nginx.conf).
# The gateway's plugin route doesn't emit CORS, so a cross-origin browser call
# is blocked — the same-origin /gw proxy is what makes it work.
#
# The token is the gateway bearer token (the value of OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN on
# the gateway). In prod it's NOT baked into the bundle — the user pastes it once
# per device in the in-app ⚙ Settings panel (stored in localStorage).

VITE_GATEWAY_URL=/gw
VITE_GATEWAY_TOKEN=<your-gateway-bearer-token>